1. Explain the concept of functional interfaces and give some examples.

A functional interface has exactly one abstract method, allowing it to be used in a lambda expression.

example of Functional Interfaces:
| Interface         | Abstract Method           | Description                                                           |
| ----------------- | ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Runnable          | void run()`               | Runs a task without returning anything                                |
| Callable<V>       | V call()`                 | Runs a task and returns a value (like `Runnable` but with result)     |
| Comparator<T>     | int compare(T o1, T o2)`  | Compares two objects for sorting                                      |


e.g.,
@FunctionalInterface
interface Calculator {
    int add(int a, int b);
}

Calculator c = (x, y) -> x + y;
System.out.println(c.add(5, 3)); // 8

